WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.310
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Thursday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.030
Here's your day in transhumanism, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.290
See it coming. In a Sydney study,

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:21.810
arm swing changed nearly 7 years before a Parkinson's diagnosis.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.540
And DeepMind's AlphaGenome 2 predicts wha

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.050
t a DNA change does in each type of cell.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.980
Experts appointed by OpenAI say its AI's proof for

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.270
part of a million-dollar physics problem checks out.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.060
Closer to home, CSIRO's AI, trained on cats,

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.930
dogs and cars, confirmed the famous black hole photo.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.600
Meanwhile,

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.170
Berkeley and NVIDIA released free tools that let teams of AI agents write and test robot programs.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.900
And AI found three brain types in kids with ADHD or anxiety,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.610
even before diagnosis.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.790
In longevity,

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:07.250
a brain-wiring pattern that sets SuperAgers apart flagged healthy older people who later declined faster.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.290
In old mice,

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.220
a week of a tiny peptide rejuvenated the ovaries and boosted litter sizes.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.860
And a single dose of a friendly gut microbe protec

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.780
ted mice with a Parkinson's gene from brain damage.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.290
Meanwhile, older patients who got delirium, a sudden confusion,

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.420
in hospital had about five times the dementia risk.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.490
On to wellbeing. Across 115 trials,

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:36.960
three antidepressants kept people well more often than Prozac.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.140
And in VR,

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:43.480
facing an avatar of the voices they hear helped 13 of 30 people with schizophrenia.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Now, the catch.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.050
Microsoft found editing under 10 neurons can turn an AI agent into a hidden sleeper agent.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.070
And a city council in Indiana voted to ban superintelligence,

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.770
though it doesn't exist yet.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.730
Out in space,

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:08.290
dust from beyond Neptune held traces of ancient water from the Solar System's birth.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:14.990
And physicists measured gravity between two silicon wafers of just 7.6 milligrams each,

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.250
the smallest yet.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:20.390
Oh, and Colorado engineers built trunk-like robots that bend,

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.680
grab and clip together into teams.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.430
From a walk to a brain scan,

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.610
we're learning to see trouble coming, and that buys us time.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.440
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.140
Live long. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
